[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831817193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-2831817193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":2831817193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oyhnp","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-26T04:03:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-26T04:03:19Z","body":"Sounds like\n- #96737","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831817193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844749724","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-2844749724","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":2844749724,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pj2-c","user":{"login":"hippogyz","id":77163339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTYzMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77163339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz","html_url":"https://github.com/hippogyz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hippogyz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T12:31:21Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T12:31:21Z","body":"Hey, use `Rid inputImage = renderSceneBuffers.GetTexture(\"render_buffers\", \"color\");` replace https://github.com/Rokojori/godot-compositor-effect-c-sharp/blob/1f88a13f1f07820ade0243ae2185654ead0459fd/PostProcessGrayscaleCS.cs#L109\n\nIt works for me. But I don't know how to get the textures of different view indice in the `for-` loop. \n\nBTW, I'm working in PostOpaque stage. But no matter gdscript/C# case, I failed to write color back to the color buffer when using MSAA. \n\nMaybe this discussion helps. https://godotforums.org/d/42152-any-way-to-write-color-buffer-in-compositoreffect-when-enabling-msaa","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844749724/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844818106","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-2844818106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":2844818106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pkHq6","user":{"login":"Rokojori","id":208519335,"node_id":"U_kgDODG3Apw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208519335?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori","html_url":"https://github.com/Rokojori","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T13:08:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T13:08:26Z","body":"Thanks a lot for the workaround for effects at the post transparent stage ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844818106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844863408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-2844863408","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":2844863408,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pkSuw","user":{"login":"Rokojori","id":208519335,"node_id":"U_kgDODG3Apw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208519335?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori","html_url":"https://github.com/Rokojori","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rokojori/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T13:38:26Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T13:39:13Z","body":"I checked the source a bit and changed it to \n\n```\n\nvar renderBufferName =  \"color\"; // \"depth\"\nvar textureView = new RDTextureView();\nvar layerView = 0;\nvar mipMapLevel = 0;\nvar numLayers = 1;\nvar numMipMaps = 1;\n\nrenderSceneBuffers.GetTextureSliceView(\n   \"render_buffers\",  renderBufferName , layerView, mipMapLevel, \n    numLayers,  numMipMaps, textureView\n);\n\n\n```\n\n\nThis works the same for me, I don't know if it is correctly affecting the possible render views.\nIn the c++ source, all texture getters and up using this:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/80a3d205f1ad22e779a64921fb56d62b893881ae/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/render_scene_buffers_rd.cpp#L414\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844863408/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3097177227","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-3097177227","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":3097177227,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64myyL","user":{"login":"Petapetilon","id":45501253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTAxMjUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45501253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon","html_url":"https://github.com/Petapetilon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Petapetilon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-21T15:09:15Z","updated_at":"2025-07-21T15:09:15Z","body":"@hippogyz  When my vulkan knowledge does not let me down: The second View should be a second layer \"get_color_layer(int index)\". So if you change the layerView to \"1\" it should give you the a second layer of the texture. Maybe you also need to increase the number of \"numLayers\" to 2.\n\n```\nvar renderBufferName =  \"color\"; // \"depth\"\nvar textureView = new RDTextureView();\nvar layerView = 1; // from 0 to 1\nvar mipMapLevel = 0;\nvar numLayers = 1;\nvar numMipMaps = 1;\n\nrenderSceneBuffers.GetTextureSliceView(\n   \"render_buffers\",  renderBufferName , layerView, mipMapLevel, \n    numLayers,  numMipMaps, textureView\n);\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3097177227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244543177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-3244543177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":3244543177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BY8zJ","user":{"login":"TomHensel","id":109302967,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoPUtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109302967?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel","html_url":"https://github.com/TomHensel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TomHensel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T09:30:14Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T10:22:40Z","body":"Hello everyone,\nI realised that you can also use the following code to get the proper color texture:\n`Rid inputImage = renderSceneBuffers.GetColorLayer(view, false);`\nSetting the msaa bool to false manually gives you the same texture as GDScript would, which doesn't make sense since it should be set to false automatically. This is probably a bug in the C# version.\nAnother bug I have found is that the` public override void _Notification(int what)` function is never called in the C# CompositorEffect, so the shader is never freed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244543177/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316126441","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-3316126441","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":3316126441,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FqBLp","user":{"login":"russelljahn","id":2547417,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NDc0MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2547417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn","html_url":"https://github.com/russelljahn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russelljahn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T17:08:21Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T17:08:21Z","body":"After porting the [greyscale CompositorEffect example](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/rendering/compositor.html) from GDScript to C#, I hit this exact same issue. Running the GDScript example on the exact same camera Compositor worked perfectly fine, tho.\n\nI was able to work around it in C# with TomHensel's [suggestion above](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-3244543177):\n```\nRid inputImage = renderSceneBuffers.GetColorLayer(view, false); // <--- Explicitly set \"msaa\" to false.\n```\n\nI'm also not seeing `public override void _Notification(int what)` trigger for CompositorEffect in C#.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316126441/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3445844074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105637#issuecomment-3445844074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105637","id":3445844074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NY2hq","user":{"login":"HEX-23","id":29618465,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjE4NDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29618465?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23","html_url":"https://github.com/HEX-23","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HEX-23/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-25T04:58:21Z","updated_at":"2025-10-25T04:58:21Z","body":"I think this is not particular to C#.\nAccording to the C++ src about creating the color and depth textures, storage bit is only present in the resolved buffer when MSAA is on. You will be able to use imageLoad/Store on get_color_layer(view, false) or get_texture('render_buffers', 'color'), but writing back into it via imageStore (when the compositor effect is set to run at any stage other than post_transparent) doesn't seem to have any effect.\nI suspect that the pipeline is not using the resolved buffer in intermediate stages, maybe you need to write into the unresolved, multisampling buffers through the use of a custom graphics pipeline. But I am not very familiar with the C++ codebase, I haven't pinned down the very piece of code responsible for these.\nSee this issue for more info: [Link](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106743#issuecomment-3445778978)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3445844074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]